	)
	(text "This schematic is based on:\nhttps://github.com/tkilla64/eurorack/blob/deeafd41/misc/crossover-filter/xover-filter_sch_v2.pdf\nBut converted from single-supply to double-supply configuration. Also with some minor extra changes.\nSo praise https://github.com/tkilla64 for the original schematic.\n\nIn ideal scenario:\n- At exactly cross-over frequency both outputs are -90° relative to the input\n- Both mains and sub outputs are ideally 0° relative to each-other at each frequency (in-phase)\n- Well below cross-over frequency sub outputs approach 0° relative to the input (in-phase relative to the input)\n- Well above cross-over frequency mains outputs approach -180° relative to the input (out-of-phase relative to the input)\n\nCrossover Frequency (Hz):\n- Fmin = 1 / (2π * (10000Ω pot max value + 3300Ω) * 220nF in farads, 220E-9) = 54Hz\n- Fmax = 1 / (2π * (0 pot min value + 3300Ω) * 220nF in farads, 220E-9) = 219Hz"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.732 282.194 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "88d076d6-a863-4f50-8f85-00048c60c363")
	)
	(text "Q = 0.5"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.396 211.074 0)
		(effects
